{
  "title": "Mentre {im:studiavo}, {pp:è arrivato} Luca",
  "translation": "While I was studying, Luca arrived",
  "topics": "The difference between the passato prossimo and the imperfetto",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "Think of a film"
      },
      "The *imperfetto* is the scenery of the film: what was going on, what things were like. The *passato prossimo* is the event: what happened, one step at a time, and is now finished.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "",
            "Imperfetto",
            "Passato prossimo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Question it answers",
              "What was it like? What was going on?",
              "What happened?"
            ],
            [
              "Length",
              "No clear start or end",
              "Finished, or a stated length of time"
            ],
            [
              "Repetition",
              "A habit: ogni giorno, di solito",
              "A counted number of times: tre volte"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "*Ieri {im:pioveva}* tells you about the weather as a background. *Ieri {pp:è arrivato} Luca* tells you an event.",
      {
        "h": "One sentence, two tenses"
      },
      "When an event interrupts something that was already going on, the background is in the *imperfetto* and the interruption in the *passato prossimo*.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Background",
            "Event"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Mentre {im:studiavo},",
              "{pp:è arrivato} Luca."
            ],
            [
              "Mentre {im:dormivo},",
              "{pp:è suonato} il telefono."
            ],
            [
              "{im:Pioveva} quando",
              "{pp:siamo usciti}."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "Two actions side by side"
      },
      "If two actions were going on at the same time, both are in the *imperfetto*: *Mentre io {im:cucinavo}, lui {im:leggeva}*. If they happen one after another, both are in the *passato prossimo*: *{pp:Sono entrato} e {pp:ho acceso} la luce*.",
      {
        "h": "A stated length of time"
      },
      "Even if an action lasted long, a stated length makes it a finished block, so use the *passato prossimo*: *{pp:Ho vissuto} a Roma per dieci anni*. *{im:Abitavo} a Roma* only says that was your situation then."
    ]
  },
